# Modern JavaScript Rules of Thumb

```text
1. Prefer const by default.

2. Use let when reassignment is required.

3. Avoid var unless you specifically need its behavior.

4. Prefer === and !== over == and !=.

5. Use arrow functions for concise callbacks.

6. Use map() when transforming arrays.

7. Use filter() when selecting array items.

8. Use reduce() when producing one accumulated value.

9. Use for...of for clean array iteration.

10. Use destructuring when it makes object access clearer.

11. Prefer CSS classes over extensive inline style manipulation.

12. Use textContent instead of innerHTML when inserting plain text.

13. Use async/await for readable asynchronous workflows.

14. Wrap fallible asynchronous operations in appropriate error handling.

15. Check response.ok when using fetch() if HTTP failures should be treated as errors.
```

